WEBVTT

00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:06.110
<i>The second half of this 
route is a winding downhill.</i>

00:00:06.920 --> 00:00:09.860
<i>He's an airhead motivated by rage.</i>

00:00:10.190 --> 00:00:13.090
<i>That's the easiest type of person to beat.</i>

00:00:13.090 --> 00:00:14.890
<i>I'll let him stay ahead for now.</i>

00:00:14.890 --> 00:00:17.450
<i>His legs will become exhausted in the 
second half, and he'll lose speed.</i>

00:00:17.900 --> 00:00:20.580
<i>But I'll strike one blow first!</i>

00:00:23.080 --> 00:00:25.110
Are you familiar with my nickname?

00:00:25.110 --> 00:00:27.080
They call me the Peak Hornet.

00:00:28.070 --> 00:00:30.630
Am I too fast? Too close?

00:00:31.040 --> 00:00:33.010
Is your answer "yes"?

00:00:35.970 --> 00:00:37.870
You're not on the road.

00:00:39.140 --> 00:00:41.460
<i>This guy will be easy.</i>

00:00:41.460 --> 00:00:44.220
<i>His eyes are full of rage.</i>

00:00:44.220 --> 00:00:48.400
<i>If his rage disrupts his pace like I expect, 
he'll lose speed in the second half!</i>

00:00:48.730 --> 00:00:50.860
<i>He moved up! He really is an airhead!</i>

00:00:50.860 --> 00:00:54.740
What should the loser's punishment be?

00:00:55.780 --> 00:00:57.950
It's not fun without one.

00:00:58.410 --> 00:01:03.000
If I win, will you be my 
assistant in the next race?

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:05.920
Since you're so big, I bet 
you block a lot of wind.

00:01:06.380 --> 00:01:08.340
What do you want, Ashikiba-san?

00:01:08.340 --> 00:01:12.100
Would you like me to apologize to 
third-years Kaneko-san and

00:01:12.100 --> 00:01:14.940
Shimozaki-san and ask them for advice?

00:01:15.460 --> 00:01:18.900
That's what you should 
be doing as a first-year.

00:01:20.790 --> 00:01:26.230
If you lose, go find the trash you threw 
on the ground before we started...

00:01:27.930 --> 00:01:29.230
and pick it up.

00:01:35.860 --> 00:01:43.450
<b><i>Yowamushi Pedal</i></b>

00:03:02.510 --> 00:03:07.010
<i>LINE.21  Limiter</i>

00:03:03.700 --> 00:03:06.110
Trash? Talk about anal retentive.

00:03:06.110 --> 00:03:08.280
Is this about keeping the planet beautiful?

00:03:08.280 --> 00:03:09.480
You must be joking.

00:03:10.450 --> 00:03:14.000
Mountains, rivers, valleys, and coastlines...

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:18.940
We use the terrain created by 
nature to ride our bicycles.

00:03:18.940 --> 00:03:22.640
We're indebted to nature. 
We should respect it.

00:03:23.380 --> 00:03:27.470
It's not something you should 
so selfishly pollute.

00:03:27.470 --> 00:03:29.090
<i>What's with this guy?</i>

00:03:29.090 --> 00:03:30.980
<i>He's annoying me.</i>

00:03:31.510 --> 00:03:35.650
No one wants to criticize 
you because of Shinkai-san.

00:03:37.080 --> 00:03:41.830
Isn't that what you want 
to shake off the most?

00:03:41.830 --> 00:03:44.450
<i>He thinks he can say whatever he wants.</i>

00:03:44.890 --> 00:03:46.700
<i>Does he think he's right?</i>

00:03:47.950 --> 00:03:49.350
<i>I have...</i>

00:03:50.820 --> 00:03:54.170
<i>my own troubles!</i>

00:03:56.250 --> 00:03:57.720
<i>No matter.</i>

00:03:57.720 --> 00:03:59.670
<i>An airhead like him would never understand.</i>

00:04:00.320 --> 00:04:02.230
<i>I'm changing my plan.</i>

00:04:02.230 --> 00:04:05.470
<i>I'll pass him and pull ahead of him!</i>

00:04:09.140 --> 00:04:10.220
<i>What's going on?</i>

00:04:10.220 --> 00:04:12.520
<i>He blocked my route as I was about to go.</i>

00:04:12.840 --> 00:04:16.160
I told you, first-year Shinkai Yuto...

00:04:16.160 --> 00:04:17.790
that I'd crush you.

00:04:19.080 --> 00:04:21.650
I'm not letting you get ahead of me!

00:04:26.010 --> 00:04:27.240
You're riding on the gutter.

00:04:27.870 --> 00:04:30.580
<i>Damn it! He's making fun of me!</i>

00:04:30.580 --> 00:04:33.790
<i>Then I'll do whatever it 
takes to get in front of him!</i>

00:04:36.360 --> 00:04:37.450
Kaneko...

00:04:37.960 --> 00:04:41.420
Kaneyan hurt his knees after riding with you.

00:04:43.320 --> 00:04:46.590
He and Yuki-chan have been climbing 
buddies since they were first-years.

00:04:46.590 --> 00:04:49.350
They used to talk about the 
Inter-High together all the time.

00:04:49.730 --> 00:04:53.850
But Kaneyan's knees probably 
won't heal in time for the Inter-High.

00:04:53.850 --> 00:04:56.090
What? Who cares?

00:04:56.090 --> 00:04:57.060
That's totally unrelated.

00:04:58.130 --> 00:05:00.280
Kenyan practices hard.

00:05:00.760 --> 00:05:03.320
He never makes excuses.

00:05:04.340 --> 00:05:08.820
Shimo knows that, so he never rides 
ahead of Kaneyan on mountains.

00:05:09.720 --> 00:05:11.860
You beat them.

00:05:12.410 --> 00:05:14.290
But is there really...

00:05:15.060 --> 00:05:17.670
nothing you can learn from Kaneda?!

00:05:19.410 --> 00:05:24.800
You just had "nobody understands my pain"
 written all over your face.

00:05:25.810 --> 00:05:28.310
How could they? Of course they don't.

00:05:29.140 --> 00:05:32.390
Because you don't even 
try to understand theirs.

00:05:32.840 --> 00:05:35.320
<i>What? What does that mean?</i>

00:05:35.320 --> 00:05:38.850
<i>Are you saying someone as physically 
blessed as you has problems?</i>

00:05:39.830 --> 00:05:42.730
You don't work hard and lack respect.

00:05:43.290 --> 00:05:47.110
If you fought against the old Kaneyan...

00:05:47.770 --> 00:05:49.950
You'd lose!

00:05:50.680 --> 00:05:51.720
<i>He's gone!</i>

00:05:52.600 --> 00:05:54.540
<i>Am I going to lose to him?</i>

00:05:55.030 --> 00:05:57.750
<i>It's just a stupid mental battle!
 A mental battle!</i>

00:05:57.750 --> 00:06:00.010
<i>I can't lose now!</i>

00:06:00.190 --> 00:06:01.950
<i>Go!</i>

00:06:02.710 --> 00:06:07.650
<i>Was he not motivated by rage?</i>

00:06:10.250 --> 00:06:14.640
<i>So he was calmly observing my 
movements and controlling me.</i>

00:06:15.300 --> 00:06:16.450
<i>Damn.</i>

00:06:16.450 --> 00:06:19.480
<i>I couldn't even see his 
back on the final bend.</i>

00:06:20.180 --> 00:06:22.560
Get up. Go pick up your trash.

00:06:23.980 --> 00:06:25.140
Yes, sir.

00:06:26.260 --> 00:06:27.770
I'll go with you.

00:06:28.840 --> 00:06:29.700
Huh?

00:06:29.700 --> 00:06:32.060
You don't have to.

00:06:32.060 --> 00:06:34.790
You'd have to climb to the 
peak again to get back there.

00:06:34.790 --> 00:06:36.520
It's my penalty.

00:06:36.950 --> 00:06:38.320
Oh, that's right.

00:06:38.950 --> 00:06:40.420
<i>He's not putting up a fight?</i>

00:06:41.960 --> 00:06:43.790
<i>Maybe he really is an airhead.</i>

00:06:44.570 --> 00:06:49.430
<i>I hate to admit it, but it's true that 
he's stronger and smarter than me.</i>

00:06:49.990 --> 00:06:55.050
<i>When he accelerated in front of me,
the pressure I felt was no laughing matter.</i>

00:06:55.720 --> 00:06:57.430
<b>Hakone Academy Bicycle Racing Club</b>

00:06:57.430 --> 00:07:01.020
<i>Kaneko-senpai told me 
about Ashikiba-san later.</i>

00:07:01.460 --> 00:07:03.620
<i>About his concerns about his height.</i>

00:07:03.620 --> 00:07:05.640
<i>About being the laundry boy.</i>

00:07:05.640 --> 00:07:08.360
<i>How he was suspended 
indefinitely from racing.</i>

00:07:08.950 --> 00:07:10.350
No, Yuto!

00:07:10.350 --> 00:07:12.160
That timing will allow our 
enemies to get ahead of us!

00:07:12.670 --> 00:07:14.930
Be patient! Watch their movements!

00:07:14.930 --> 00:07:15.700
Yes, sir!

00:07:16.820 --> 00:07:18.680
You cut your bangs two centimeters.

00:07:18.680 --> 00:07:20.030
You could tell?

00:07:20.030 --> 00:07:21.510
He can tell?

00:07:22.250 --> 00:07:24.350
Did you hear about Yuto?

00:07:24.350 --> 00:07:28.710
He apologized to Haraguchi 
for breaking his phone.

00:07:28.710 --> 00:07:31.030
I can tell from watching him at practice.

00:07:31.030 --> 00:07:34.260
He's fierce, but he's changed.

00:07:35.080 --> 00:07:38.850
<i>Until then, I thought of everyone 
I rode with as an opponent.</i>

00:07:39.940 --> 00:07:44.370
<i>I came to enjoy riding with Ashikiba-san.</i>

00:07:51.810 --> 00:07:53.740
Hakone Academy's ace is losing speed!

00:07:53.740 --> 00:07:55.490
But it's a critical moment!

00:07:55.490 --> 00:07:58.890
Didn't he just win the mountain line?

00:07:58.890 --> 00:08:00.160
That's why his legs are exhausted!

00:08:00.160 --> 00:08:02.740
#16 is dropping back to help him!

00:08:02.740 --> 00:08:05.420
They're falling behind the two in front!

00:08:05.420 --> 00:08:09.410
They're only thirty meters behind,
but at the finish line of a road race,

00:08:09.410 --> 00:08:11.240
that's an overwhelming distance!

00:08:11.240 --> 00:08:14.090
There's just one kilometer 
left to the finish line!

00:08:12.220 --> 00:08:14.090
<b>National High School Sports Tournament
Cycling Road Race
 Distance to Day 2 Finish Line</b>

00:08:14.420 --> 00:08:16.080
<i>He lost speed?</i>

00:08:16.080 --> 00:08:18.510
<i>Did Ashikiba-san lose focus for a moment?</i>

00:08:19.050 --> 00:08:22.800
<i>No, it' because of his all-out attack 
for the mountain line.</i>

00:08:22.800 --> 00:08:27.520
<i>After fighting so hard, his legs 
couldn't last until the finish line.</i>

00:08:29.370 --> 00:08:32.310
<i>Too bad, Hakone Academy.</i>

00:08:32.310 --> 00:08:34.320
<i>The mountain line or the finish line...</i>

00:08:34.780 --> 00:08:40.040
<i>It's obvious which is more valuable 
when you weigh them against each other.</i>

00:08:40.870 --> 00:08:43.160
<i>You made a mistake.</i>

00:08:43.160 --> 00:08:48.590
<i>The two of you can fight for third.</i>

00:08:49.130 --> 00:08:50.340
Ashikiba-san!

00:08:51.380 --> 00:08:52.970
I'm starting to feel it in my legs.

00:08:52.970 --> 00:08:55.470
I couldn't keep up with the increase in pace.

00:08:55.470 --> 00:08:58.520
What is this? Why?

00:08:58.520 --> 00:09:01.890
You tried to show off by 
saying you hadn't given up.

00:09:02.400 --> 00:09:05.330
But you're exhausted.

00:09:06.420 --> 00:09:08.650
If only I'd...

00:09:11.110 --> 00:09:12.480
After him, Yuto.

00:09:13.320 --> 00:09:15.850
...gone like you told me to.

00:09:16.570 --> 00:09:18.370
If only I'd trusted you.

00:09:18.770 --> 00:09:20.370
We're coming up on the finish line.

00:09:20.370 --> 00:09:22.620
Just go and get it.

00:09:23.410 --> 00:09:24.950
I'm sorry.

00:09:25.510 --> 00:09:29.630
Yuto, we can't change the past.

00:09:30.820 --> 00:09:31.500
So...

00:09:35.300 --> 00:09:37.260
So I feinted.

00:09:37.260 --> 00:09:38.340
Feinted?

00:09:38.900 --> 00:09:40.870
After taking the mountain line,

00:09:40.870 --> 00:09:44.060
I put on an act that Sohoku and 
Kyoto Fushimi wouldn't notice.

00:09:44.790 --> 00:09:49.690
I deliberately slowed down, fell behind
 my assistant, and made him pull.

00:09:50.470 --> 00:09:55.380
I made them think I was the ace 
taking today's finish line.

00:09:56.340 --> 00:10:01.060
I made them think Hakone Academy
was finished, so they'd let down their guard.

00:10:02.170 --> 00:10:07.250
When I decided to attack in the mountains, 
I knew I'd be exhausting my legs.

00:10:08.050 --> 00:10:11.250
I knew I had to plan for what was next.

00:10:12.090 --> 00:10:16.720
I knew immediately who else 
could go for the finish line.

00:10:18.440 --> 00:10:20.310
I was a little worried.

00:10:20.920 --> 00:10:23.140
After all, he's a climber.

00:10:23.140 --> 00:10:25.100
But my concerns were immediately swept away

00:10:25.670 --> 00:10:29.480
because his brother was a great sprinter.

00:10:30.500 --> 00:10:32.060
You want me to take the 
second day's finish line?

00:10:32.770 --> 00:10:36.340
I ended up tricking you, too.

00:10:36.900 --> 00:10:37.970
Sorry.

00:10:39.050 --> 00:10:40.450
Zip up your jersey.

00:10:41.490 --> 00:10:43.450
I know you can do it!

00:10:44.210 --> 00:10:45.430
Hey, Yuto.

00:10:45.430 --> 00:10:47.660
Why don't you practice with us on the flats?

00:10:48.020 --> 00:10:51.590
The upperclassmen want to see you sprint.

00:10:51.590 --> 00:10:54.720
I'll pass. I'm not Hayato-kun.

00:10:54.720 --> 00:10:56.300
I'm a climber.

00:10:57.090 --> 00:10:58.850
<i>I'm Yuto.</i>

00:10:58.850 --> 00:11:02.680
<i>But Ashikiba-san's telling me to go.</i>

00:11:03.690 --> 00:11:05.120
Zip it up, Yuto.

00:11:05.120 --> 00:11:06.850
There's not much time or distance left.

00:11:06.850 --> 00:11:09.180
You'll take today's finish line.

00:11:09.750 --> 00:11:12.690
Zip up your jersey, Shinkai Yuto!

00:11:15.290 --> 00:11:15.940
Yes, sir!

00:11:17.640 --> 00:11:18.920
<i>Ashikiba-san!</i>

00:11:18.920 --> 00:11:21.200
<i>This time, I'll go!</i>

00:11:21.560 --> 00:11:22.330
What's going on?

00:11:22.330 --> 00:11:23.780
Their ace moved up!

00:11:23.780 --> 00:11:24.630
No way!

00:11:24.630 --> 00:11:27.010
They're having a first-year 
race for the finish line?

00:11:27.010 --> 00:11:28.370
Isn't he a climber?

00:11:28.370 --> 00:11:30.570
No, there's an old saying!

00:11:30.570 --> 00:11:34.330
All six of Hakone Academy's 
members are the ace!

00:11:34.700 --> 00:11:37.600
I'll close this thirty-meter gap.

00:11:37.600 --> 00:11:39.340
When I give the signal, you move up.

00:11:39.340 --> 00:11:42.520
Until then, I'll block the wind for you!

00:11:42.520 --> 00:11:43.220
Yes, sir!

00:11:43.850 --> 00:11:44.990
Let's go, Yuto!

00:11:44.990 --> 00:11:45.600
Yes, sir!

00:11:46.090 --> 00:11:48.600
Ashikiba is accelerating!

00:11:49.270 --> 00:11:51.480
<i>The finish line. I'm taking the finish line.</i>

00:11:51.970 --> 00:11:53.650
<i>The finish line sprint!</i>

00:11:56.410 --> 00:11:58.280
<i>What? What is this?</i>

00:11:59.290 --> 00:12:01.970
<i>Nervousness? No...</i>

00:12:02.420 --> 00:12:04.740
<i>What is this? What on earth is this?</i>

00:12:05.690 --> 00:12:08.200
<i>What's making my cells buzz with excitement?</i>

00:12:08.620 --> 00:12:12.080
Hakone Academy's catching up
 at the very last second!

00:12:12.450 --> 00:12:17.430
Hakone Academy's sending #16 as their 
ace to the second day's finish line!

00:12:18.330 --> 00:12:20.550
<i>What? They're catching up?</i>

00:12:20.550 --> 00:12:24.510
<i>I thought Hakone Academy had fallen, 
but they've switched out their ace!</i>

00:12:24.510 --> 00:12:26.760
<i>Their final ace is #16!</i>

00:12:27.190 --> 00:12:29.860
<i>No way. #16?</i>

00:12:29.860 --> 00:12:32.970
<i>Did they just come up with that?</i>

00:12:33.310 --> 00:12:37.670
<i>No, that's not what the 
big guy's eyes are saying.</i>

00:12:37.670 --> 00:12:39.820
<i>He planned this.</i>

00:12:40.290 --> 00:12:45.280
<i>Ashikiba-kun's been fooling us since then.</i>

00:12:47.140 --> 00:12:48.740
Are you ready, Yuto?

00:12:49.070 --> 00:12:51.290
Go, Yuto!

00:12:53.010 --> 00:12:54.040
Yuto—

00:12:54.490 --> 00:12:55.860
It's okay.

00:12:56.310 --> 00:12:58.420
Sorry, Ashikiba-san.

00:12:58.420 --> 00:13:00.420
I'm not sure why...

00:13:01.060 --> 00:13:03.840
but all the cells in my body 
are buzzing with excitement.

00:13:03.840 --> 00:13:06.180
I can't calm down.

00:13:06.180 --> 00:13:09.570
I know! I'll go right away!

00:13:13.900 --> 00:13:16.680
Go!

00:13:14.940 --> 00:13:16.680
Hakone Academy's attacking!

00:13:16.680 --> 00:13:17.190
He's so fast!

00:13:17.190 --> 00:13:19.210
<i>Damn! Damn!</i>

00:13:19.210 --> 00:13:21.400
<i>This feeling is insane.</i>

00:13:23.220 --> 00:13:26.360
<i>Every time my speed increases, 
my cells start screaming.</i>

00:13:27.110 --> 00:13:28.320
<i>This is ecstasy!</i>

00:13:29.590 --> 00:13:33.770
Thanks for waiting,
Midousuji-san and Imaizumi-san!

00:13:35.770 --> 00:13:39.460
With 600 meters remaining, 
Hakone Academy caught up!

00:13:39.460 --> 00:13:41.710
It's a three-way race again!

00:13:43.080 --> 00:13:45.500
#16, Shinkai Yuto...

00:13:45.500 --> 00:13:47.340
You're in a good mood.

00:13:48.210 --> 00:13:54.080
To think they'd send a first-year 
climber in place of their useless ace.

00:13:54.080 --> 00:13:56.390
Now this is a surprise.

00:13:57.060 --> 00:13:58.610
<i>He caught up.</i>

00:13:58.610 --> 00:14:02.570
<i>What can a climber do in a 
race for the finish line?</i>

00:14:04.360 --> 00:14:06.090
<i>I'm glad he caught up.</i>

00:14:06.570 --> 00:14:10.200
<i>If I'd pulled for Yuto on the 
downhill instead of pretending,</i>

00:14:10.200 --> 00:14:14.410
<i>they would've realized he 
was the ace and crushed us.</i>

00:14:15.140 --> 00:14:16.790
<i>I'm brilliant.</i>

00:14:17.290 --> 00:14:18.920
<i>But that face he made when he left...</i>

00:14:19.520 --> 00:14:23.750
<i>I've never seen Yuto so happy.</i>

00:14:24.070 --> 00:14:27.630
The ninety-degree turn that's 500 meters
 before the finish line is just ahead!

00:14:30.370 --> 00:14:33.370
All three are braking hard 
out of intense acceleration!

00:14:33.370 --> 00:14:34.640
It's a braking contest!

00:14:34.980 --> 00:14:36.210
They're still neck-and-neck!

00:14:36.210 --> 00:14:38.140
After the corner, it's a straight 
line to the finish line!

00:14:38.140 --> 00:14:41.440
All three of them want to pull ahead here!

00:14:41.950 --> 00:14:43.820
Who will make it through first?

00:14:45.250 --> 00:14:46.650
No one's giving any ground!

00:14:47.900 --> 00:14:48.890
A super close-quarters battle!

00:14:48.890 --> 00:14:50.090
You can hear them clashing!

00:14:52.530 --> 00:14:53.870
Gross!

00:14:54.550 --> 00:14:57.040
They pulled out of the corner 
in the same formation!

00:14:57.830 --> 00:15:01.670
<i>#16 kept up with our high-risk cornering.</i>

00:15:02.610 --> 00:15:05.200
<i>It seems he's no ordinary climber.</i>

00:15:05.200 --> 00:15:07.840
<i>Hakone Academy can't be underestimated.</i>

00:15:08.500 --> 00:15:13.040
<i>So #16 has steeled his resolve.</i>

00:15:13.040 --> 00:15:16.560
<i>He was smiling during the entire corner.</i>

00:15:17.210 --> 00:15:20.310
<i>And I thought Hakone Academy 
was out of the race.</i>

00:15:20.710 --> 00:15:25.530
<i>Shinkai's brother. </i>That<i> Shinkai's brother...</i>

00:15:25.530 --> 00:15:30.440
<i>Fine. I'll make them taste despair again.</i>

00:15:31.960 --> 00:15:33.130
<i>This time...</i>

00:15:33.130 --> 00:15:35.530
<i>This time, at the finish line!</i>

00:15:36.070 --> 00:15:39.380
<i>Ashikiba-san, I'm going to win.</i>

00:15:39.380 --> 00:15:40.410
<i>My answer is...</i>

00:15:41.480 --> 00:15:42.290
Yes!

00:15:43.310 --> 00:15:44.600
400 meters!

00:15:44.600 --> 00:15:45.190
Remaining!

00:15:45.190 --> 00:15:46.540
To the finish line!

00:15:48.000 --> 00:15:51.220
<b>Inter-High Road Race</b>

00:15:48.610 --> 00:15:49.630
<i>I see it!</i>

00:15:49.630 --> 00:15:51.220
<i>The second day's finish line gate!</i>

00:15:51.860 --> 00:15:52.800
<i>All that's left...</i>

00:15:56.470 --> 00:15:59.220
<i>is this 400-meter straightaway!</i>

00:15:59.220 --> 00:16:02.310
#16, Shinkai Yuto, is attacking!

00:16:02.650 --> 00:16:03.490
<i>What was that?</i>

00:16:03.490 --> 00:16:07.110
<i>He dropped behind Midousuji for a 
second and accelerated around him.</i>

00:16:07.690 --> 00:16:10.360
<i>Did he use Midousuji to 
block the wind for a moment?</i>

00:16:10.890 --> 00:16:12.470
<i>I can't predict what he'll do.</i>

00:16:12.470 --> 00:16:14.360
<i>His movements are too tricky.</i>

00:16:14.360 --> 00:16:16.370
<i>And he's always one step ahead.</i>

00:16:17.740 --> 00:16:20.130
<i>Is he going for the finish line...</i>

00:16:20.130 --> 00:16:22.080
<i>...from 400 meters?</i>

00:16:22.080 --> 00:16:23.620
You're not getting away!

00:16:28.710 --> 00:16:30.460
Wow, I'm impressed.

00:16:30.460 --> 00:16:33.400
Where are you going, #16?

00:16:33.400 --> 00:16:35.010
That was some nice acceleration,

00:16:35.010 --> 00:16:37.990
but it's a bit early to be 
racing for the finish line.

00:16:38.520 --> 00:16:39.730
Are you in a hurry?

00:16:46.840 --> 00:16:48.420
It was a feint.

00:16:48.420 --> 00:16:49.910
<i>A feint?</i>

00:16:49.910 --> 00:16:54.650
<i>He did that on purpose, to see how we'd react?</i>

00:16:54.650 --> 00:17:00.650
<i>When he attacked, I thought he was making 
a desperate attempt for the finish line.</i>

00:17:00.650 --> 00:17:02.000
<i>He really is</i>

00:17:02.000 --> 00:17:05.310
<i>Shinkai Hayato's younger brother.</i>

00:17:05.310 --> 00:17:08.630
<i>I'll need to raise my threat level to six.</i>

00:17:09.070 --> 00:17:12.440
Was 400 too early, Imaizumi-san?

00:17:12.440 --> 00:17:13.300
Then...

00:17:13.850 --> 00:17:15.490
How about 300?

00:17:19.220 --> 00:17:20.470
<i>He's attacking!</i>

00:17:20.470 --> 00:17:22.770
<i>Is he starting the second round now?</i>

00:17:25.170 --> 00:17:26.310
<i>What's with this guy?</i>

00:17:26.310 --> 00:17:28.520
<i>The usual rules of the finish line
 sprint don't apply to him.</i>

00:17:31.150 --> 00:17:32.540
We caught you.

00:17:32.540 --> 00:17:33.280
What's the rush?

00:17:33.280 --> 00:17:36.860
I thought I had it that time.

00:17:36.860 --> 00:17:38.870
You really are fast.

00:17:39.450 --> 00:17:42.390
<i>First it was a feint made 
to look like a sprint.</i>

00:17:42.390 --> 00:17:45.870
<i>Then it was a sprint made 
to look like a feint.</i>

00:17:45.870 --> 00:17:48.750
Shinkai Yuto!

00:17:48.750 --> 00:17:51.130
What is it, Midousuji-san?

00:17:54.050 --> 00:17:56.030
You're contemptuous!

00:17:56.030 --> 00:17:56.990
You're a bit close.

00:17:56.990 --> 00:17:58.460
You're two-faced!

00:17:58.460 --> 00:18:01.010
Getting close to people is my specialty.

00:18:01.630 --> 00:18:04.310
And you're gross!

00:18:06.310 --> 00:18:08.940
What's that? A compliment?

00:18:09.880 --> 00:18:14.820
<i>Looks like I'll have to raise 
my threat level to ten.</i>

00:18:14.820 --> 00:18:18.490
<i>He won't even look away after all of that.</i>

00:18:18.490 --> 00:18:20.660
<i>He fully intends to fight.</i>

00:18:23.350 --> 00:18:26.880
I wasn't expecting to find it here.

00:18:26.880 --> 00:18:30.040
I thought it disappeared last year.

00:18:30.400 --> 00:18:33.340
The ghost of Shinkai-kun!

00:18:33.340 --> 00:18:36.170
No, I'm alive.

00:18:37.540 --> 00:18:39.720
I've got legs.

00:18:39.720 --> 00:18:41.930
It is time for round three?

00:18:43.960 --> 00:18:45.610
There's 250 meters left!

00:18:45.610 --> 00:18:48.710
Kyoto Fushimi and Hakone Academy 
are getting ready to sprint!

00:18:50.650 --> 00:18:53.110
No, Sohoku attacked a moment earlier!

00:18:53.480 --> 00:18:56.230
Imaizumi is entering the 
finish line sprint in the lead!

00:18:56.670 --> 00:18:57.860
<i>Now.</i>

00:18:57.860 --> 00:19:00.720
<i>My body reacted before I could think.</i>

00:19:00.720 --> 00:19:02.000
<i>I'll keep going like this!</i>

00:19:02.000 --> 00:19:03.660
<i>I'll stay ahead of them and win!</i>

00:19:05.720 --> 00:19:08.410
<i>Now! Go, Imaizumi Shunsuke!</i>

00:19:11.160 --> 00:19:12.420
<i>Seriously?</i>

00:19:12.420 --> 00:19:13.950
<i>He was a second faster!</i>

00:19:13.950 --> 00:19:15.750
<i>He just barely got ahead!</i>

00:19:16.190 --> 00:19:19.150
<i>But he's Weakizumi! But he's Crackizumi!</i>

00:19:19.150 --> 00:19:22.590
<i>But he's Chirpizumi! But he's...</i>

00:19:23.400 --> 00:19:26.140
<i>No, no. That doesn't matter now.</i>

00:19:26.520 --> 00:19:30.270
<i>There are pests in front of me!</i>

00:19:30.270 --> 00:19:32.360
<i>I'll knock them aside!</i>

00:19:32.360 --> 00:19:34.230
<i>That's all that matters!</i>

00:19:34.740 --> 00:19:36.770
<i>I'll win!</i>

00:19:37.460 --> 00:19:41.150
<i>I've fought for the finish line 
in countless races until now.</i>

00:19:41.150 --> 00:19:47.040
<i>But I've only ever won when my body 
reacted instinctively, like it did now.</i>

00:19:47.040 --> 00:19:49.540
<i>I'll shake off Midousuji and Shinkai.</i>

00:19:49.540 --> 00:19:51.210
<i>I'll ride in the front!</i>

00:19:51.210 --> 00:19:54.330
<i>So jump! Jump, jump!</i>

00:19:54.330 --> 00:19:56.790
My limiter!

00:19:57.140 --> 00:19:58.720
Imaizumi-kun's coming!

00:19:58.720 --> 00:19:59.790
He's in front!

00:19:59.790 --> 00:20:00.670
He attacked first!

00:20:00.670 --> 00:20:03.510
Go, Imaizumi-san!

00:20:05.640 --> 00:20:07.600
<i>Jump, jump!</i>

00:20:08.140 --> 00:20:09.410
<i>Imaizumi-kun...</i>

00:20:09.830 --> 00:20:14.100
I feel like I haven't gone all-out
 since I became a second-year.

00:20:14.100 --> 00:20:17.470
Last year, I had seniors. 
I was unconstrained.

00:20:17.470 --> 00:20:18.570
But this year...

00:20:19.240 --> 00:20:24.150
It feels like I've had a limiter 
installed here the whole time.

00:20:24.710 --> 00:20:26.120
<i>His limiter...</i>

00:20:26.120 --> 00:20:28.370
They're catching up!

00:20:28.690 --> 00:20:31.330
<i>Fall off! Off, off!</i>

00:20:36.770 --> 00:20:40.630
<i>A limiter? Don't be ridiculous, 
Imaizumi Shunsuke.</i>

00:20:41.180 --> 00:20:42.750
<i>This is nothing.</i>

00:20:42.750 --> 00:20:46.010
<i>Compared to what they did, this is nothing!</i>

00:20:46.440 --> 00:20:48.640
<i>If it won't come off, then I'll force it off.</i>

00:20:49.050 --> 00:20:56.550
<i>The whole team carried this jersey this 
far by pushing themselves to their limits!</i>

00:20:58.730 --> 00:21:03.610
Fall off, limiter!

00:21:09.930 --> 00:21:11.240
Sohoku's accelerating!

00:21:11.240 --> 00:21:11.870
He's so fast!

00:21:11.870 --> 00:21:13.250
What is that sprint?

00:21:15.350 --> 00:21:18.420
<i>Charge straight ahead, Imaizumi Shunsuke!</i>

00:21:18.770 --> 00:21:20.410
Why is he so intense?

00:21:20.410 --> 00:21:23.050
Has he always been that passionate?

00:21:23.050 --> 00:21:25.780
Imaizumi's always full of passion.

00:21:25.780 --> 00:21:28.260
He's the most dependable guy on the team.

00:21:28.660 --> 00:21:31.430
And the strongest.

00:21:32.720 --> 00:21:35.230
Win, Imaizumi!

00:21:36.230 --> 00:21:38.100
Of course!

00:21:38.950 --> 00:21:42.070
<i>He's back to his usual strong-willed self.</i>

00:21:42.570 --> 00:21:45.030
150 meters remaining!

00:23:20.690 --> 00:23:23.460
Yuto, you cut your bangs two centimeters.

00:23:23.460 --> 00:23:26.090
You could tell? I cut them myself.

00:23:26.740 --> 00:23:27.420
It looks good.

00:23:29.050 --> 00:23:30.530
<b>Several Days Later</b>

00:23:31.410 --> 00:23:33.430
Yuto, you cut your bangs again.

00:23:35.480 --> 00:23:37.090
No, I didn't.

00:23:36.780 --> 00:23:39.930
<i>NEXT LINE  Three Powerhouses</i>

00:23:37.770 --> 00:23:38.760
It looks good.

00:23:39.930 --> 00:23:44.940
This is a work of fiction. All characters and organizations
 appearing in this work are fictional. In this work,
 characters sometimes engage in dangerous activities.
 While riding bicycles on actual roads,
 please follow all traffic laws and ride safely.

00:23:44.940 --> 00:23:50.250
<b>Don't miss the next episode</b>
